<% content_for :title, "Acceptable Use Policy" %>

<main class="policy">
  <div class="policy__wrap">
    <header class="policy__head">
      <p class="policy__kicker">Salato</p>
      <h1 class="policy__title">Acceptable Use Policy</h1>
      <p class="policy__meta">Last updated <%= Date.current.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %></p>
    </header>

    <section class="policy__intro">
      <p>
        Salato is a platform for selling and managing tickets to events. This policy
        explains what you may and may not do when you use Salato, whether you are an
        event organiser selling tickets or an attendee buying them. By creating an
        account, publishing an event, or purchasing a ticket, you agree to use Salato
        in line with this policy. We may update it from time to time; the current
        version always lives at this page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="who">
      <h2>Who this applies to</h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to everyone who uses Salato: organisers, their staff and
        scanners, attendees, and anyone who accesses the platform or the tickets it
        produces. Organisers are responsible for making sure their own team follows
        these rules.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="allowed">
      <h2>What you can use Salato for</h2>
      <p>Salato is intended for lawful, genuine event ticketing. You may:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Create events and sell tickets to real events you are authorised to organise.</li>
        <li>Set your own ticket types, prices and refund terms, within this policy and our Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy.</li>
        <li>Collect only the attendee information you need to admit people to your event.</li>
        <li>Scan and verify tickets at your event using the QR codes Salato issues.</li>
        <li>Buy tickets for yourself or others and receive them by email and WhatsApp.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="prohibited">
      <h2>What you must not do</h2>
      <p>You may not use Salato to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Sell tickets to events you are not authorised to organise, or to events that do not genuinely exist.</li>
        <li>Sell anything other than event tickets and directly related add-ons. Salato is not a marketplace for physical goods, and physical goods may not be listed or sold through it.</li>
        <li>Break any applicable law, or sell tickets to any event that is itself unlawful.</li>
        <li>Sell tickets to events promoting violence, hate, harassment, or discrimination on the basis of race, ethnicity, religion, gender, disability, sexual orientation, or any other protected characteristic.</li>
        <li>Facilitate fraud, money laundering, or the financing of any illegal activity.</li>
        <li>Sell access to sexual services, or to any event that exploits or endangers minors.</li>
        <li>Sell alcohol, tobacco, drugs, weapons, or any controlled or age-restricted product as if Salato were a shop for them.</li>
        <li>Misrepresent an event — its date, venue, line-up, capacity, or what a ticket includes.</li>
        <li>Deceive buyers about refund terms, fees, or who is running the event.</li>
        <li>Resell, duplicate, forge, or tamper with tickets or QR codes, or attempt to reuse a single-use ticket.</li>
        <li>Chargeback abuse, or make payments you know or suspect to be fraudulent.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="platform">
      <h2>Protecting the platform</h2>
      <p>To keep Salato safe and reliable for everyone, you must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access another person's account, or share credentials that let someone impersonate an organiser or admin.</li>
        <li>Probe, scan, or test the security of the platform without our written permission.</li>
        <li>Introduce malware, or attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorised access to Salato or its infrastructure.</li>
        <li>Scrape, harvest, or bulk-collect data from the platform, including attendee data, beyond what you are entitled to as an organiser for your own events.</li>
        <li>Interfere with the payment, ticket generation, scanning, or notification systems.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="data">
      <h2>Attendee data</h2>
      <p>
        Organisers receive attendee information so they can run their events. If you
        are an organiser, you must use that information only to deliver and manage the
        event the attendee bought a ticket for. You must not sell attendee data, or
        use it for unrelated marketing without the attendee's consent, and you must
        keep it secure. You remain responsible for complying with Kenya's Data
        Protection Act and any other data protection law that applies to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="payments">
      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Payments on Salato are processed by our payment partner. Each organiser
        receives funds into their own connected settlement account, and Salato takes
        only its platform commission. Salato does not hold organiser funds, does not
        operate wallets or stored balances, and does not enable transfers of value
        between users. You must not use Salato to move money for any purpose other
        than paying for tickets to a genuine event.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="enforcement">
      <h2>What happens if you break this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we believe you have breached this policy, we may — depending on how serious
        the breach is — warn you, remove an event or listing, suspend your ability to
        sell tickets, hold or reverse a payout, or close your account. Where an event
        has clearly not been delivered as advertised, we may suspend the organiser and
        support affected buyers with refunds through our payment partner. Serious
        breaches, including fraud or anything that endangers people, may be reported to
        the relevant authorities. We may act immediately and without notice where there
        is a risk to attendees, buyers, or the platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="policy__section" id="report">
      <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
      <p>
        If you come across an event, organiser, or ticket on Salato that you think
        breaks this policy, tell us at
        <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a>. Include the event name
        and any details that help us look into it. We review every report.
      </p>
    </section>

    <footer class="policy__foot">
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@salato.app">hello@salato.app</a>.
      </p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</main>

<style>
  .policy {
    --ink: #150D3A;
    --violet: #7620B1;
    --orange: #FC8027;
    --mist: #F7F4FB;
    background: var(--mist);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: "Inter Tight", "Trebuchet MS", system-ui, sans-serif;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem) 1.25rem clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
  }
  .policy__wrap { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .policy__head { padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1); margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .policy__kicker {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: .8rem; letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--violet);
    margin: 0 0 .75rem;
  }
  .policy__title {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.05;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 3.2rem);
    margin: 0 0 .9rem;
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--violet), var(--orange));
    -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent;
  }
  .policy__meta { margin: 0; color: rgba(21,13,58,.6); font-size: .95rem; }
  .policy__intro p, .policy__section p, .policy__foot p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .policy__intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  .policy__section { margin-bottom: 2.75rem; }
  .policy__section h2 {
    font-family: "Outfit", "Trebuchet MS", sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 .8rem;
    padding-left: .85rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--orange);
  }
  .policy__section p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .policy__section ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  .policy__section li { line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: .55rem; }
  .policy a { color: var(--violet); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .policy a:hover { color: var(--orange); }
  .policy__foot {
    margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.75rem;
    border-top: 2px solid rgba(21,13,58,.1);
    color: rgba(21,13,58,.7); font-size: .95rem;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .policy__section h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; }
  }
</style>
